    "head_commit_message": "feat(sim): the groups as one crate pass\n\nFormationGroups.step is one crate pass (`groups::pass::step`, binding\n`groups_step`): the groups fallen behind split off, each new group's\nsquad opened in the crate with the battle's next issued id (\"split\"),\nthen the groups at ease form up and each meeting lands there: a group\ntaken in (\"merged\") or units sent back to the command they started\nunder, behind its back row (\"rejoined\"). FormationGroups wraps the slots\nopened and mirrors its unit lists; GroupSplit and the `group_split` and\n`group_form_up` bindings are removed. A split group used to be squad 0 in\nthe crate; it now holds its own id, so outcomes change.\n\nSpec 39 step 8b5-xxx.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011AyPi4NFPZw6WGxxQgoNPL",
